LAW ON PROTECTION AGAINST DOMESTIC VIOLENCE (TITLE AMENDED - SG, ISSUE 102 OF 2009, IN FORCE FROM 22.12.2009)
Promulgated SG Issue 27 of 29 March 2005, amended SG Issue 82 of 10 October 2006, amended SG Issue 102 of 22 December 2009, amended SG Issue 99 of 17 December 2010, supplemented SG Issue 50 of 3 July 2015, amended SG Issue 24 of 22 March 2019, amended SG Issue 101 of 27 December 2019, amended and supplemented SG Issue 66 of 1 August 2023, amended and supplemented SG Issue 69 of 11 August 2023.
Draft: 354-01-22/17.04.2003
Chapter One.
GENERAL PROVISIONS
Art. 1. (1) (Amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) This law regulates:
1. the rights of persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk;
2. the measures for protection against domestic violence;
3. the bodies and mechanisms for implementing state policy for prevention and protection against domestic violence and the interaction between them;
4. the programmes for prevention and specialised services for providing protection, assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk;
5. the proceedings for imposing measures for protection against domestic violence;
6. the measures for the application of Regulation (EU) No 606/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 June 2013 on mutual recognition of protection measures in civil matters (OJ, L 181/4 of 29 June 2013), hereinafter referred to as "Regulation (EU) No 606/2013".
(2) (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The State conducts a consistent policy in the field of domestic violence through coordination, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of policies and measures for prevention and protection against domestic violence.
(3) (Supplemented - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, former para. 2, amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The measures under this law do not exclude the civil, administrative-penal and criminal liability of the perpetrator.
Art. 1a. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The purpose of the law is to provide rapid and effective protection and to ensure assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk, and to exercise a preventive and deterrent effect on the perpetrator of the violence.
Art. 2. (Amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009) (1) (Amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024, supplemented - SG, Issue 69 of 2023) Domestic violence is any act of physical, sexual, psychological or economic violence, as well as an attempt at such violence, forced restriction of personal life, personal freedom and personal rights, committed against persons who are in a kinship relationship, who are or have been in a family relationship or in de facto cohabitation or in an intimate relationship.
(2) (Amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) Psychological violence against a child is also considered to be any domestic violence committed in his or her presence.
(3) (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The acts under para. 1 and 2 may be committed through action or omission.
Art. 3. Protection under this law may be sought by any person who has suffered from domestic violence committed by:
1. a spouse or former spouse;
2. (supplemented - SG, Issue 69 of 2023) a person with whom he or she is or has been in de facto cohabitation or in an intimate relationship;
3. a person from whom he or she has a child;
4. an ascendant;
5. a descendant;
6. (amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009) a person with whom he or she is in kinship by collateral line up to and including the fourth degree;
7. (amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009) a person with whom he or she is or has been in kinship by affinity up to and including the third degree;
8. (amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) a guardian, trustee, person to whom care for the child has been entrusted, or person to whom the child has been entrusted;
9. (new - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024, amended - SG, Issue 69 of 2023) a person who is a relative by direct or collateral line up to and including the fourth degree, of the person with whom he or she is or has been in de facto cohabitation or in an intimate relationship;
10. (new - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, supplemented - SG, Issue 69 of 2023) a person with whom the parent is or has been in de facto cohabitation or in an intimate relationship;
11. (new - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) a person who is a spouse or former spouse of the parent.
Art. 4. (1) In case of domestic violence, the victim has the right to seek protection from the court.
(2) (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) At the request of the victim, state and municipal bodies, medical establishments and legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence are obliged within 24 hours to forward to the relevant district court the application for initiating proceedings for issuing a protection order.
(3) (Amended - SG, Issue 82 of 2006, amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, former para. 2 - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) In cases where there is evidence of danger to the life or health of the victim, he or she may also submit an application to the bodies of the Ministry of the Interior for taking measures in accordance with the Law on the Ministry of the Interior.
(4) (Former para. 3 - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) At the request of the victim, every doctor is obliged to issue a document in which he or she certifies in writing the injuries or traces of violence established by him or her.
Art. 5. (1) (Amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009) The measures for protection against domestic violence are:
1. obliging the perpetrator to refrain from committing domestic violence;
2. removal of the perpetrator from the jointly inhabited dwelling for the period determined by the court;
3. (supplemented - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, supplemented - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) prohibition on the perpetrator from approaching the victim, the dwelling, the workplace and the places of social contacts and recreation of the victim under conditions and for a period determined by the court;
4. (new - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) prohibition on the perpetrator from making contact with the victim in any form, including by telephone, through electronic or ordinary mail and fax, as well as through any other means and communication systems under conditions and for a period determined by the court;
5. (former item 4, supplemented - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) temporary determination of the child's place of residence with the victim parent or with the parent who did not commit the violence, under conditions and for a period determined by the court, if this does not contradict the interests of the child;
6. (former item 5, supplemented - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) obliging the perpetrator of the violence to attend specialised programmes for overcoming aggression and anger management;
7. (former item 6, amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) referring victims to specialised services for protection, assistance and support or recovery programmes;
8. (new - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) referring child victims to specialised services for protection, assistance and support for children who are victims or witnesses of violence.
(2) (Amended - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, amended and supplemented - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The measures under para. 1, items 2 - 5 shall be imposed for a period of three to 18 months, deducting the period of validity of the measures under an order for immediate protection issued under Art. 18 and 19.
(3) (New - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) In proceedings under this law, the court shall carry out a mandatory assessment for imposing the measure under para. 1, item 5, when the victim and the perpetrator have a child.
(4) (Former para. 3 - SG, Issue 102 of 2009, in force from 22.12.2009, amended - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The court may order as a protective measure that the regime of personal relations, determined under the procedure of the Family Code, between the child and the parent who is the perpetrator of domestic violence, be carried out for the period under para. 2 in a protected environment provided in a specialised service under this law or provided by a provider of social services at the child's current address or place of residence, under the supervision of a psychologist or social worker.
Art. 6. (Repealed - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024)
Chapter One "a".
NATIONAL COUNCIL FOR PREVENTION AND PROTECTION AGAINST DOMESTIC VIOLENCE (NEW - SG, ISSUE 66 OF 2023, IN FORCE FROM 01.08.2023)
Art. 6a. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.08.2023) (1) A National Council for Prevention and Protection against Domestic Violence, hereinafter referred to as "the National Council", shall be established at the Council of Ministers.
(2) The National Council is a specialised permanent collective and consultative body for implementing state policy on prevention and protection against domestic violence through coordination, monitoring and evaluation of policies and measures for prevention and protection against domestic violence.
(3) The Chairman of the National Council is a Deputy Prime Minister appointed by the Council of Ministers. The Deputy Chairman of the National Council is the Minister of Justice.
(4) The composition of the National Council includes the Minister of the Interior, the Minister of Labour and Social Policy, the Minister of Health, the Minister of Education and Science, the Minister of Youth and Sports, a representative of the Supreme Court of Cassation, the Chairperson of the State Agency for Child Protection, the Executive Director of the Social Assistance Agency, the Executive Director of the National Association of Municipalities in the Republic of Bulgaria.
(5) The composition of the National Council includes representatives of non-profit legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence. The organisations that represent these members of the Council and related persons may not participate with projects for funding under the procedure of Art. 6e, para. 6.
(6) In the meetings of the National Council, at the invitation of the Chairman, the Ombudsman of the Republic of Bulgaria, Members of Parliament, representatives of the judicial authorities, representatives of academic circles, representatives of legal entities and international organisations with representations in the country that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence, heads of other state bodies, representatives of local self-government and local administration bodies, of professional and civil organisations, other officials and experts may participate.
(7) The administrative-technical, organisational, expert and financial servicing of the National Council shall be carried out by the administration of the Council of Ministers.
(8) The Council of Ministers shall adopt rules for the structure, organisation and activity of the National Council.
(9) The conditions and procedure for the selection of non-profit legal entities under para. 5 shall be determined in the rules under para. 8.
Art. 6b. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.08.2023) (1) The National Council:
1. determines the priorities in policies in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence;
2. carries out coordination, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of policies and measures in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence;
3. develops and updates a coordination mechanism for assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence, and submits it for adoption by the Council of Ministers, monitors its effective functioning and gives instructions and recommendations on its application;
4. develops a national programme for prevention and protection against domestic violence based on the identified priority activities for funding and submits it for adoption by the Council of Ministers, making proposals for its updating when necessary;
5. requests and receives information from state bodies, legal entities and others that are related to prevention and protection against domestic violence;
6. creates and maintains a national information system for cases of domestic violence committed on the territory of the country, or in relation to Bulgarian citizens abroad who have sought assistance and support, and a list of legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence under the procedure of this law, in compliance with the requirements of the Personal Data Protection Act;
7. summarises and analyses the results of the implementation of policies in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence and proposes measures to increase their effectiveness;
8. publishes and disseminates statistical information in connection with domestic violence in compliance with the requirements of the Statistics Act and the Personal Data Protection Act;
9. organises the conduct of information, awareness-raising and training campaigns on issues related to domestic violence;
10. develops and updates draft strategies, programmes and plans in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence and monitors and reports on their implementation;
11. gives opinions and makes proposals for amending existing and adopting new normative acts in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence;
12. develops draft normative acts in connection with prevention and protection against domestic violence and submits them to the Council of Ministers through the Chairman of the National Council;
13. approves methodological guidelines and participates jointly with other representatives of organisations, institutions and judicial bodies in the development of documents related to risk assessment under this law;
14. carries out international cooperation with international organisations and institutions with activities in the field of prevention and protection against domestic violence, exchanging information and good practices;
15. approves the procedures for selection of activities for prevention of domestic violence and specialised services for protection against domestic violence, financed under the procedure of Art. 6e, para. 6, and exercises control over the fulfilment of the conditions under the funding contract;
16. approves training programmes for employees to perform functions in connection with prevention and protection against domestic violence;
17. maintains and develops a national helpline for persons who have suffered from domestic violence and are at risk;
18. monitors and evaluates the impact of measures for prevention and protection against domestic violence.
(2) The Chairman of the National Council shall submit an annual report on its activities to the Council of Ministers.
Chapter One "b".
INTERACTION OF THE NATIONAL COUNCIL WITH BODIES AND ORGANISATIONS (NEW - SG, ISSUE 66 OF 2023, IN FORCE FROM 01.01.2024)
Art. 6c. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) (1) For carrying out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence, the National Council shall interact with the executive authorities, the judicial authorities, the local self-government and local administration bodies and the legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence.
(2) The interaction under para. 1 shall be carried out through:
1. exchange of information on identified cases of violence, risk assessment, referral to competent bodies and/or organisations, determination of measures for protection and support, applications for protection against domestic violence and regarding the implementation of measures and/or
2. carrying out joint actions in prevention and protection against domestic violence.
Art. 6d. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) (1) The interaction for protection, assistance and support of victims of domestic violence shall be carried out under the conditions and according to the procedure of a coordination mechanism for assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence.
(2) The coordination mechanism under para. 1 regulates the basic procedures for interaction between the executive authorities, the local self-government and local administration bodies and the legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence under the procedure of this law. The interaction shall be carried out at the following stages:
1. notification and referral:
a) identification of cases of violence;
b) risk assessment from the point of view of the life and health of the victim with a view to adequate planning of protection measures and for a coordinated response;
c) referral for use of specialised services;
2. determination of protection measures in case of:
a) direct and immediate danger of domestic violence;
b) risk;
3. measures for long-term support after cessation of violence:
a) psycho-social counselling and psychotherapeutic work;
b) development of skills for realisation on the labour market and for realisation in the social environment;
c) social counselling, advocacy and active social work.
Chapter One "c".
NATIONAL INFORMATION SYSTEM (NEW - SG, ISSUE 66 OF 2023, IN FORCE FROM 03.08.2024)
Art. 6e. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 03.08.2024) (1) The National Council shall create and maintain a National Information System for Prevention and Protection against Domestic Violence, in which data on cases of domestic violence committed on the territory of the country, or in relation to Bulgarian citizens abroad who have sought assistance and support, shall be stored, hereinafter referred to as the "National Information System".
(2) The National Information System contains data on:
1. acts of domestic violence;
2. victims, perpetrators and the relationships between them;
3. the type of violence - physical, psychological, sexual, economic, restriction of rights and others;
4. the duration of the violence;
5. the harm caused to the victim;
6. the history of violence;
7. applications submitted for issuing a protection order, an order for immediate protection or requests of the prosecutor under the procedure of Art. 8, para. 2;
8. measures imposed under this law, the Law on the Ministry of the Interior, the Child Protection Act and social services provided under the procedure of the Social Services Act in relation to persons who have suffered from domestic violence;
9. legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence under the procedure of this law;
10. services used under the procedure of this law.
(3) The National Council shall ensure the registration, storage and maintenance in an up-to-date state of the data under para. 2.
(4) The information subject to entry in the National Information System, the procedure for collection and provision, and the organisation and functioning of the system and the level of access shall be determined by the implementing regulations of the law.
(5) The executive authorities, the judicial authorities, the local self-government and local administration bodies and the legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection against domestic violence under the procedure of this law shall provide the National Council with the necessary data under para. 2 according to a procedure determined in the implementing regulations of the law.
(6) Officials from the Ministry of the Interior, the Social Assistance Agency, the State Agency for Child Protection and the judicial authorities shall have the right of access to the data in the National Information System.
(7) Personal data in the system under para. 1 shall be stored for a period of no more than twenty years.
(8) For the purposes of the system under para. 1, the National Council shall have the right of access to data on perpetrators of domestic violence in the Unified Information System for Combating Crime under Art. 378 of the Judicial System Act according to a procedure determined by the implementing regulations of this law.
Chapter One "d".
PROGRAMMES FOR PREVENTION AND SPECIALISED SERVICES FOR PROTECTION AGAINST DOMESTIC VIOLENCE (NEW - SG, ISSUE 66 OF 2023, IN FORCE FROM 01.01.2024)
Chapter One "d".
PROGRAMMES FOR PREVENTION AND SPECIALISED SERVICES FOR PROTECTION AGAINST DOMESTIC VIOLENCE
Art. 6f. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) (1) The State shall create conditions for the implementation of programmes for prevention of domestic violence and specialised services for protection, assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence and are at risk.
(2) The executive authorities, the National Institute of Justice and the local self-government and local administration bodies shall organise training for persons who carry out activities under this law.
(3) The executive authorities, the local self-government and local administration bodies and the legal entities that carry out activities for prevention and protection of persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk, under the procedure of this law, shall develop, organise the implementation and implement the programmes and services provided for in Art. 5, para. 1, items 6 - 8.
(4) The Council of Ministers shall adopt a three-year national programme for prevention and protection against domestic violence by 31 March of the relevant year.
(5) The funds for financing the fulfilment of obligations under the national programme under para. 4 shall be determined on the basis of medium-term three-year financial forecasts prepared by the respective executive authorities having commitments to the implementation of activities from the programme.
(6) By the State Budget Act of the Republic of Bulgaria for the relevant year, funds shall be determined in the budget of the Council of Ministers for financing projects of the persons under para. 3, provided that they carry out activities under this law, for the development and implementation of:
1. programmes for prevention of domestic violence concerning:
a) work with the judicial authorities;
b) work with the bodies of the Ministry of the Interior, including training of police officers and other employees of law enforcement bodies for identifying cases of domestic violence, on protocols for response and application of the relevant legislation; the programme shall be adopted by the Ministry of the Interior;
c) training in educational institutions for preventing domestic violence and promoting equality and respect between the sexes; the programme shall be adopted by the Ministry of Education and Science;
d) training of persons who carry out prevention and protection under the law;
e) monitoring of the application of the law;
f) preparation and conduct of information campaigns, seminars and conferences;
2. specialised services for providing protection, assistance and support to persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk, which include:
a) a national helpline for persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk;
b) social, psychological and legal counselling and specialised programmes for recovery and/or protection of persons or children who are victims of domestic violence or witnesses, in a counselling centre;
c) social, psychological and legal counselling and specialised programmes for recovery and/or protection of persons or children who are victims of domestic violence or witnesses, in a sheltered dwelling;
3. specialised programmes for overcoming aggression and anger management for perpetrators of domestic violence, which include social and psychological counselling.
(7) The procedures for selection of legal entities that carry out prevention of domestic violence under the procedure of this law, the conditions and procedure for financing, reporting and control of prevention activities shall be determined by the implementing regulations of the law in compliance with the rules on state aid.
Art. 6g. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) (1) A person who has suffered from domestic violence shall be provided with the following specialised services independently or as a complex:
1. a national helpline for persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk;
2. a counselling centre for persons who have suffered from domestic violence;
3. a sheltered dwelling.
(2) The specialised services under para. 1 shall be provided according to the wishes and personal choice of persons who have suffered from domestic violence or are at risk, and shall be free of charge. The services shall be provided regardless of whether the victims have expressed consent to cooperate in identifying the perpetrator of the domestic violence.
(3) The use of a specialised service under para. 1 does not exclude the use of other services.
Art. 6h. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) A person who has committed domestic violence shall be provided with a specialised programme for overcoming aggression and anger management. The programme may be part of a complex of specialised services or may be provided independently.
Art. 6i. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) When using a specialised service or programme under the procedure of this law, the persons under Art. 6g and 6h shall be provided with appropriate and timely information in a language understandable to them.
Art. 6j. (New - SG, Issue 66 of 2023, in force from 01.01.2024) The conditions, procedure and minimum standards for providing specialised services and programmes for protection against domestic violence under the procedure of this law, as well as their financing and control, shall be regulated by the implementing regulations of the law.
Chapter Two.
PROCEEDINGS FOR IMPOSING MEASURES FOR PROTECTION AGAINST DOMESTIC VIOLENCE (TITLE AMENDED - SG, ISSUE 102 OF 2009, IN FORCE FROM 22.12.2009)

