§ 1

(New - SG, No. 66 of 2023, effective from 01.01.2024) For the purposes of this law:
1. "National helpline for persons affected by domestic violence or at risk, with a single harmonised telephone number" is a free telephone line with national coverage and a single harmonised telephone number for reporting cases of domestic violence, informing, counselling, referring persons affected by domestic violence or persons at risk, while respecting confidentiality and anonymity for the persons. The telephone line is accessible around the clock, seven days a week, every day of the year.
2. "Counselling centre for persons affected by domestic violence" is an independent service or a complex of interdisciplinary specialised services for adults and/or children affected by domestic violence, which provides psychological, social and legal assistance and which are aimed at ensuring support for the victims simultaneously with the use or after the use of other specialised services.
3. "Sheltered housing" is a specialised service for the protection of adults and their children affected by domestic violence, which consists of temporary accommodation in a safe environment.
4. "Related persons" within the meaning of Art. 6a, para. 5 are:
a) persons in whose management body the same legal or natural person participates;
b) persons in whose supreme body the same legal or natural person participates, which can impose or prevent the taking of decisions;
c) persons, one of which is a member of the National Council and whose representative in the National Council is in hierarchical dependence on the other by virtue of an employment relationship;
d) persons, one of which is a member of the National Council and has received remuneration from the other by virtue of a civil law relationship in a total amount exceeding BGN 10,000 during the last twelve months from the date of their election as a member of the National Council;
e) persons, one of which is a member of the National Council and has received a donation and/or grant funding from the other in a total amount exceeding BGN 10,000 during the last twelve months from the date of their election as a member of the National Council;
f) persons, one of which exercises control over the other;
g) persons whose activity is controlled by a third person or by its subsidiary legal entity.
5. "Control" within the meaning of letters f) and g) of item 4 exists when the controlling party:
a) holds directly or indirectly or by virtue of an agreement with another person more than half of the votes in the supreme body of another person, or
b) has the possibility to determine directly or indirectly more than half of the members of the management or supreme body of another person, or
c) can otherwise exercise decisive influence on decision-making in connection with the activity of the legal entity.
6. (new - SG, No. 69 of 2023) "Intimate relationship" represents a totality of voluntary and lasting personal, intimate and sexual relations between two natural persons of male and female sex, regardless of whether they share one household and whose emergence, content and termination are not subject to legal regulation by another law. Lasting within the meaning of the preceding sentence are relations with a duration of at least 60 days.
